# Real CRITICAL findings in the runtime image's Debian bookworm base
# packages, each with no available fix as of the date recorded below.
# Confirmed by building a throwaway copy of this image with `apt-get
# upgrade` added to the runtime stage and re-scanning it: the installed
# version of every one of these five packages was unchanged, matching
# Trivy's own `Status` column for each (affected / fix_deferred /
# will_not_fix -- no fixed version exists yet, not merely "not installed
# here"). That `apt-get upgrade` was NOT kept in Dockerfile.app itself:
# tests/infrastructure/test_dockerfile.py enforces that the runtime stage
# never runs a package manager at all (a real, intentional minimal-
# attack-surface design, not an oversight this phase should override for
# a change that verifiably fixes nothing). This file accepts a real,
# currently-unfixable residual risk transparently instead (Constitution
# non-fabrication rule: silencing or lowering the scan's severity
# threshold would misrepresent "no fix exists yet" as "no vulnerability
# exists"). Re-run the container scan after any base-image digest bump;
# remove an entry once its `Fixed Version` is no longer empty.
#
# Recorded 2026-09-16 (Phase 18), python:3.11-slim-bookworm@sha256:528257d4...

# libsqlite3-0 3.40.1-2+deb12u2 -- Status: affected (no fixed version yet).
# Not reachable from this codebase: no service parses attacker-controlled
# SQLite files: Postgres is this repo's only relational store.
CVE-2025-7458

# perl-base 5.36.0-7+deb12u3 -- Status: affected. Perl is a Debian base-image
# transitive dependency (apt/dpkg tooling); this repository has no Perl
# code and never invokes an interpreter on untrusted input.
CVE-2026-13221
CVE-2026-8376

# perl-base 5.36.0-7+deb12u3 -- Status: fix_deferred (Debian's own
# maintainers marked it not urgent enough to backport yet). Same
# unreachability rationale as above.
CVE-2026-42496

# zlib1g 1:1.2.13.dfsg-1 -- Status: will_not_fix (Debian will not patch this
# release). The affected path (zipOpenNewFileInZip4_6) is a ZIP-*writing*
# API; this codebase's own S3/object-store code only reads, and MinIO/S3
# operations here never shell out to zlib's CLI-adjacent write path.
CVE-2023-45853
